- We know that, too.

89
00:03:31,294 --> 00:03:33,880
Dayoung, you've got hot-girl energy.

90
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:36,007
I went for soft smoky eyes.

91
00:03:36,091 --> 00:03:37,801
You're glowing and glittering.

92
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:42,305
Actually, my goal today was
not to look too much older than you.

93
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:44,975
I asked my makeup artist
for the trendy idol makeup.

94
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:47,561
You two have such striking features.

95
00:03:47,644 --> 00:03:50,397
- Your features are far more striking.
- Oh, no.

96
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:53,442
- Are you sure? They're so strong.
- You've got that cat vibe.

97
00:03:53,525 --> 00:03:56,194
SHE'S THE LITTLE GUINEA PIG
No, Wonhee's not a cat girlie.

98
00:03:56,278 --> 00:03:57,654
That's the look she's going for.

99
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,906
- Really?
- I wouldn't call it that,

100
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:03,994
but the corners of my eyes point up,
so I think I look more like a cat.

101
00:04:04,453 --> 00:04:05,912
FANGIRLING FOR THE MILLIONTH TIME

102
00:04:05,996 --> 00:04:08,373
- Dayoung, you did a makeover.
- Yes.

103
00:04:08,457 --> 00:04:10,792
- What was the point that you focused on?
- Me?

104
00:04:10,876 --> 00:04:13,795
Well, I paid special attention

105
00:04:14,504 --> 00:04:16,715
to hair care.

106
00:04:16,798 --> 00:04:18,216
Hair and scalp.

107
00:04:18,842 --> 00:04:20,427
- Can I feel your hair?
- Sure.

108
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,762
I see what you meant.

109
00:04:21,845 --> 00:04:24,556
I went all in on keeping
my hair and scalp healthy.

110
00:04:24,639 --> 00:04:26,850
I focused a lot on hair styling.

111
00:04:27,058 --> 00:04:28,602
- Hair styling...
- Yeah.

112
00:04:28,685 --> 00:04:31,563
- Are you wearing no extensions?
- No, this is all me.

113
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:33,732
May I touch it, please?

114
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:36,067
- Oh, my.
- Goodness.

115
00:04:36,151 --> 00:04:37,110
HAIR APPRECIATION TIME

116
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:39,070
- So healthy.
- Oh, my.

117
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:39,988
JUST LIKE MONKEYS

118
00:04:40,071 --> 00:04:42,240
Do you enjoy water sports?

119
00:04:42,324 --> 00:04:43,241
Nope.

120
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:46,036
Really?

121
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:50,332
Hear me out.
Seriously, we're here to see you.

122
00:04:50,415 --> 00:04:51,792
- Really?
- Yeah.

123
00:04:51,875 --> 00:04:52,793
But it's water sports day.

124
00:04:52,876 --> 00:04:54,169
- I'm not skipping out.
- Really?

125
00:04:54,252 --> 00:04:57,380
- What a relief.
- I'll do whatever you want, Princess.

126
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:58,799
"Princess"?

127
00:04:58,882 --> 00:05:00,425
Do you like water sports?

128
00:05:00,509 --> 00:05:01,802
- I love them.
- Really?

129
00:05:01,885 --> 00:05:03,929
My headcanon is that
I was a mermaid in a past life.

130
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:05,722
- A princess like Ariel?
- Yes.

131
00:05:06,348 --> 00:05:07,474
Such a different reaction.

132
00:05:07,557 --> 00:05:09,476
When I told my dad about this,

133
00:05:09,726 --> 00:05:12,771
he said that there are
more sea creatures than mermaids.

134
00:05:12,854 --> 00:05:14,481
He basically called me a fish.

135
00:05:15,190 --> 00:05:16,775
No way, you're the princess.

136
00:05:16,858 --> 00:05:18,360
BOO, DAD

137
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:20,737
She just booed her dad. So cute.

138
00:05:20,821 --> 00:05:22,322
Lighten up the princess's mood.

139
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:24,157
OKAY, THUMBS-UP FOR YOU, DAD

140
00:05:24,241 --> 00:05:26,326
So you're not a fan of water sports.

141
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:27,327
Can I ask why?

142
00:05:27,410 --> 00:05:29,788
First off, I don't know how to swim.

143
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:31,665
But with a life jacket

144
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:33,959
- or things like tubes,
- We've got some here.

145
00:05:34,042 --> 00:05:35,335
I can have fun just fine.

146
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:36,586
Okay, that's nice.

147
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:39,256
- I like them.
- Really? Hooray.

148
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:41,508
But I prefer indoor pools
like Caribbean Bay.

149
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,093
INDOOR POOLS PREFERRED

150
00:05:43,176 --> 00:05:45,720
- Sadly, we have an outdoor shoot today.
- How unfortunate.

151
00:05:45,804 --> 00:05:47,973
What do you do during the summer break?

152
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:51,434
- I've always had to work in the summer.
- She's right.

153
00:05:51,518 --> 00:05:54,563
Right, now I think about it,
your group has that summery vibe.

154
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,439
I don't think we ever got a summer break.

155
00:05:56,523 --> 00:05:59,192
With so many festivals and events
in the summer,

156
00:05:59,276 --> 00:06:01,152
- idols don't really get a break.
- So true.

157
00:06:01,236 --> 00:06:02,571
Everyone else gets one,

158
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:05,657
- and we work to give them a good time.
- Right, we entertain them.

159
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:07,659
- Their joy keeps us energized.
- Exactly.

160
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:09,369
- That's our summer break.
- Right.

161
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:10,662
Do you like summer?

162
00:06:10,745 --> 00:06:11,621
No.

163
00:06:11,705 --> 00:06:13,373
I have my reasons.

164
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:17,794
I hate the fact that I can't avoid
getting sticky and clammy.

165
00:06:17,878 --> 00:06:19,170
- We're opposites.
- Really?

166
00:06:19,254 --> 00:06:21,798
I enjoy the sticky
and clammy feel of it all.

167
00:06:21,882 --> 00:06:23,884
This might sound odd, but bear with me.

168
00:06:23,967 --> 00:06:27,596
I love the heat of the car
left under the scorching sun.

169
00:06:27,679 --> 00:06:28,513
What?

170
00:06:28,597 --> 00:06:29,973
You really are an odd one.

171
00:06:30,307 --> 00:06:31,141
Do you agree?

172
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:32,058
OF COURSE NOT

173
00:06:32,142 --> 00:06:35,562
The blast of heat when you open the door--

174
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:37,355
The seats are burning hot.

175
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:39,733
You can feel the heat
spread through your body.

176
00:06:39,816 --> 00:06:40,942
I love the sensation.

177
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:43,653
It's so annoying.
I'd groan and grumble, too.

178
00:06:43,737 --> 00:06:44,738
HATES THE BURN

179
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:48,074
- I turn on the heated seat.
- Not the seat ventilation?

180
00:06:48,158 --> 00:06:49,326
Who does that in summer?

181
00:06:49,409 --> 00:06:50,702
- I do.
- The heater...

182
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:51,912
I just don't get it.

183
00:06:51,995 --> 00:06:54,080
I don't like wearing
multiple layers in winter.

184
00:06:54,164 --> 00:06:56,333
The cold seeping into your bones
is the worst.

185
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:58,877
It makes my hands swell,
and I don't like it.

186
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,046
I love the vibe of summer.

187
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:03,381
I love that blazing summer heat.

188
00:07:03,465 --> 00:07:05,258
It's nice to wear light
and comfortable clothes.

189
00:07:05,342 --> 00:07:06,718
- You get her, right?
- No.

190
00:07:06,801 --> 00:07:08,637
I haven't got the faintest clue.

191
00:07:08,720 --> 00:07:09,888
Do you like Southeast Asia?

192
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:11,014
Sure, I love the region.

193
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:12,098
Do you prefer colder places?

194
00:07:12,182 --> 00:07:13,224
To be honest,

195
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:15,685
I can bear the heat as long as it's dry.

196
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:17,896
It's the humidity I can't stand.

197
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,648
I don't like humidity, either.

198
00:07:19,731 --> 00:07:21,149
Which country is your favorite?

199
00:07:21,232 --> 00:07:24,194
Well, I've always wanted to go to Hawaii.

200
00:07:24,277 --> 00:07:25,111
That's so you.

201
00:07:25,195 --> 00:07:27,781
- You'd look so cute with flowers.
- I know.

202
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:29,950
DANCE OF JOY

203
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:33,036
THE HAPPIEST DUO OF THE WORLD

204
00:07:33,495 --> 00:07:36,122
- You'd look so pretty with flowers.
- Thank you.

205
00:07:36,206 --> 00:07:37,415
A special treat for you two.

206
00:07:37,499 --> 00:07:39,042
- Oh, she's so cute.
- Right?

207
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,502
This is amazing.

208
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,796
I WANT TO SQUEEZE THIS CUTIE

209
00:07:42,879 --> 00:07:44,381
- Let's both take her home.
- Deal.

210
00:07:44,464 --> 00:07:46,549
- We'll share her.
- A pigtail each.

211
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:49,219
- Excuse me?
- We'd get half of her each.

212
00:07:49,302 --> 00:07:50,762
Do you like theme park rides?

213
00:07:50,845 --> 00:07:52,430
- I sure do.
- I love them.

214
00:07:52,514 --> 00:07:54,557
Oh, I love them, too.

215
00:07:54,641 --> 00:07:56,393
- So you're an active person.
- Seems like it.

216
00:07:56,476 --> 00:07:58,520
- I think I am.
- Me too.

217
00:07:58,603 --> 00:08:01,147
- I love drop towers and bungee jumping.
- Bungee jumping?

218
00:08:01,231 --> 00:08:02,899
I haven't tried it yet. Have you tried it?

219
00:08:02,983 --> 00:08:04,818
- Yeah.
- How about you?

220
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:07,821
Probably, but I don't remember.

221
00:08:07,904 --> 00:08:09,322
I can't remember, but I bet I did it.

222
00:08:09,406 --> 00:08:11,282
We did all sorts of things, didn't we?

223
00:08:11,366 --> 00:08:13,660
For the third-generation idols like us,

224
00:08:13,743 --> 00:08:16,162
- it was a rite of passage for us.
- Yes, that's right.

225
00:08:16,246 --> 00:08:17,497
FASCINATED

226
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,290
What were some
of the most exciting activities?

227
00:08:19,374 --> 00:08:22,752
Bungee jumping and paragliding.

228
00:08:22,836 --> 00:08:24,087
What about you?

229
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:26,631
For me, it's the drop tower.
It was so terrifying.

230
00:08:26,715 --> 00:08:27,841
My gosh.

231
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,343
The one in Daegu's Eworld, especially.

232
00:08:30,427 --> 00:08:33,221
Eworld is located on a sloping hill,

233
00:08:33,304 --> 00:08:35,015
and the drop tower is on top.

234
00:08:35,098 --> 00:08:36,933
- My gosh.
- It was so frightening.

235
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:39,853
- "Nerves of steel, <i>Strong Heart</i>!"
- So cute.

236
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,980
HAHAHA

237
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:44,774
I totally sounded like an oldie, didn't I?

238
00:08:44,858 --> 00:08:46,026
3RD-GENERATION IDOL CRASHES OUT

239
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:47,902
Please edit that out!

240
00:08:47,986 --> 00:08:49,821
- Be chill, okay?
- Hang on.

241
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:52,699
That was a first.

242
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,826
- She's never heard of that before.
- Seriously?

243
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:56,661
Don't you know the show, <i>Strong Heart</i>?

244
00:08:56,745 --> 00:08:58,121
No, I know the show.

245
00:08:58,204 --> 00:09:01,291
But no one's used that phrase
as a compliment to me.

246
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:03,209
"Wonhee deserves the title <i>Strong Heart</i>!"

247
00:09:03,293 --> 00:09:04,753
I want to try the water sports now.

248
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:05,879
- Okay.
- All right.

249
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:07,005
- Shall we?
- Okay.

250
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:08,298
- Let's go.
- All right.

251
00:09:08,381 --> 00:09:09,591
