752
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:56,842
- You're defining your generation.
- Totally.

753
00:27:56,925 --> 00:28:00,345
- "Defining"?
- You definitely are.

754
00:28:00,429 --> 00:28:02,014
It's so reassuring to hear that.

755
00:28:02,097 --> 00:28:03,432
DEPENDABLE NEW FRIENDS

756
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:06,185
- So cute.
- Have you made good friends on this show?

757
00:28:06,268 --> 00:28:07,603
- I did!
- Really?

758
00:28:07,686 --> 00:28:09,438
You two are prime examples.

759
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:12,524
It feels like the production crew
carefully picked guests

760
00:28:12,608 --> 00:28:17,905
who'd click with me
and give me great advice.

761
00:28:17,988 --> 00:28:20,073
- How many friends have you made so far?
- So far?

762
00:28:20,490 --> 00:28:22,284
Twelve, I believe.

763
00:28:22,367 --> 00:28:23,702
ACTUALLY, 10 FRIENDS

764
00:28:23,785 --> 00:28:25,454
You're the baddie
with the biggest friend group.

765
00:28:25,537 --> 00:28:26,747
BADDIE WITH THE MOST FRIENDS

766
00:28:26,830 --> 00:28:28,957
- So cute.
- I debuted pretty quickly.

767
00:28:29,041 --> 00:28:32,127
My members trained longer,
so they already knew other idols.

768
00:28:32,211 --> 00:28:33,670
I've been jealous of that.

769
00:28:33,754 --> 00:28:35,839
But this show helped me make
friends in the industry.

770
00:28:35,923 --> 00:28:37,216
All in all, I loved it.

771
00:28:37,299 --> 00:28:40,093
I mean, I got to meet you two, too.

772
00:28:40,177 --> 00:28:44,097
I'm such a girl's girl,
so I've loved every minute of it.

773
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:45,891
Wasn't it ever stressful?

774
00:28:45,974 --> 00:28:47,643
Honestly, I'm grateful for everything.

775
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:51,396
I feel so lucky to meet
amazing people every shoot.

776
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:53,357
- How admirable.
- We're proud of you.

777
00:28:53,440 --> 00:28:55,734
- You figured it out so fast.
- Our little guinea pig has grown up.

778
00:28:55,817 --> 00:28:58,237
Seriously, you grasped it so fast.

779
00:28:58,320 --> 00:29:00,364
You two have worked
on a lot of variety shows, too.

780
00:29:00,447 --> 00:29:01,531
Wasn't it hard?

781
00:29:01,615 --> 00:29:03,909
When I first started out,
they were so hard.

782
00:29:03,992 --> 00:29:08,747
Unless I had my members with me,
I could barely say anything on camera.

783
00:29:08,830 --> 00:29:12,459
I'm more relaxed now,
thanks to the experiences so far.

784
00:29:13,335 --> 00:29:15,379
That's not a problem for you, though.

785
00:29:15,462 --> 00:29:18,257
I always feel
like I need to keep things moving.

786
00:29:18,340 --> 00:29:20,717
- Like you need to do something?
- Yeah.

787
00:29:20,801 --> 00:29:23,679
And when it gets awkward
among the cast members...

788
00:29:23,762 --> 00:29:27,349
- You don't like awkward silence?
- No, I don't.

789
00:29:27,432 --> 00:29:32,312
Whenever we wrap up,
I always leave thinking I did too much.

790
00:29:32,396 --> 00:29:36,483
But you need those mistakes
to find the right balance.

791
00:29:36,566 --> 00:29:39,611
Try as many things as you can.
Experience is the best teacher.

792
00:29:39,695 --> 00:29:42,072
Even embarrassing memories
will be helpful.

793
00:29:42,155 --> 00:29:43,865
How was the day for you two?

794
00:29:43,949 --> 00:29:45,450
STILL AWKWARD, EVEN IN THE FINALE

795
00:29:45,534 --> 00:29:48,328
She's so freaking cute!

796
00:29:48,412 --> 00:29:50,622
You want our feedback? You did great.

797
00:29:50,706 --> 00:29:53,834
- But it's funny how the sky cleared up.
- It's nice.

798
00:29:53,917 --> 00:29:57,254
- It's the perfect ending.
- Suddenly, it's all brighter.

799
00:29:57,337 --> 00:29:59,631
- You're glowing, girl.
- You two are dazzling.

800
00:29:59,715 --> 00:30:02,050
I enjoy working on variety shows

801
00:30:02,134 --> 00:30:05,762
because it brings people together,
just like it brought us together.

802
00:30:05,846 --> 00:30:08,640
We got a chance to hang out.

803
00:30:08,724 --> 00:30:10,809
I got to meet you
and really get to know you.

804
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:13,478
I feel the same.
I got to meet incredible people.

805
00:30:13,562 --> 00:30:15,480
Oh, you're so sweet.

806
00:30:15,564 --> 00:30:17,316
- Let's just take her home.
- I should.

807
00:30:17,399 --> 00:30:20,986
To be honest,
I didn't know about the water sports.

808
00:30:21,069 --> 00:30:23,363
When they said I'd get to meet you,
I just went,

809
00:30:23,447 --> 00:30:25,907
"Count me in. I'd be there."

810
00:30:25,991 --> 00:30:27,367
You didn't read the proposal, right?

811
00:30:27,451 --> 00:30:29,161
- Not at first.
- See?

812
00:30:29,244 --> 00:30:31,163
She didn't read the script.

813
00:30:31,246 --> 00:30:34,708
I only found out about the water sports
a few days ago.

814
00:30:34,791 --> 00:30:39,713
I said yes because I'd get to meet you.

815
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:42,257
Thanks to you, I got to try something new.

816
00:30:42,341 --> 00:30:46,887
And I was very happy
we could be here for you on the finale.

817
00:30:46,970 --> 00:30:50,849
What's more,
I got to see the real you today.

818
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:53,852
And you charmed me even more.

819
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:57,356
Every guest has been an amazing mentor.

820
00:30:57,439 --> 00:30:59,274
Every shoot helps me
work through something.

821
00:30:59,358 --> 00:31:00,776
I'm so grateful to you two,

822
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:03,153
and I owe so much to the production crew.

823
00:31:03,236 --> 00:31:05,697
All I can say is thank you.

824
00:31:05,781 --> 00:31:08,658
Why don't we take a boat ride
along the river one last time?

825
00:31:08,742 --> 00:31:10,202
- Sure.
- Sounds lovely.

826
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:11,953
<i>- Let's go.</i>
<i>- Let's go.</i>

827
00:31:14,956 --> 00:31:17,542
- Congrats on turning 20, Wonhee.
- Thank you.

828
00:31:17,626 --> 00:31:19,628
Congrats, you're an adult now.

829
00:31:19,711 --> 00:31:22,964
YAY

830
00:31:23,924 --> 00:31:26,510
- Right in the heart of Seoul.
- I know.

831
00:31:27,761 --> 00:31:28,929
So pretty.

832
00:31:29,012 --> 00:31:31,765
A TASTE OF FREEDOM ON THE HANGANG RIVER

833
00:31:31,848 --> 00:31:34,559
I'm so happy to be here with you.

834
00:31:34,643 --> 00:31:36,395
- So cute.
- The way you speak...

835
00:31:36,478 --> 00:31:38,230
After everything we did today...

836
00:31:38,313 --> 00:31:40,065
Are you still up for raising me?

837
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:41,983
WHY DO YOU KEEP ASKING?
Of course.

838
00:31:42,067 --> 00:31:45,695
You don't even have to ask.
My answer is always yes.

839
00:31:45,779 --> 00:31:47,155
Even if I ask to go swimming in the rain?

840
00:31:47,239 --> 00:31:48,657
That's not a problem.

841
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:50,367
I'm so touched.

842
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:54,454
Oh, right. There's this signature question

843
00:31:54,538 --> 00:31:56,581
I ask all my guests.

844
00:31:56,665 --> 00:31:57,541
- Which is?
- What is it?

845
00:31:57,624 --> 00:31:59,793
What's your advice for me?

846
00:31:59,876 --> 00:32:01,920
Twenty-year-old Wonhee.

847
00:32:02,003 --> 00:32:06,341
I hope you make your mark on the world.

848
00:32:07,134 --> 00:32:08,593
- Do whatever you want to do.
- Go, me!

849
00:32:08,885 --> 00:32:13,098
I'll keep Dayoung's advice in mind
and do my best.

850
00:32:13,181 --> 00:32:14,141
What about you, SinB?

851
00:32:14,224 --> 00:32:16,268
- Twenty-year-old Wonhee.
- Yes?

852
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:20,021
Even the "fake" version of yourself
is still a version of you.

853
00:32:20,105 --> 00:32:24,359
Be bold and try whatever you want to.

854
00:32:24,693 --> 00:32:28,405
I hope you dive in with confidence
and without fear.

855
00:32:28,864 --> 00:32:31,324
GOOD LUCK, LITTLE PRINCESS

856
00:32:31,533 --> 00:32:36,621
I'm happy to wrap up the finale
with such heartwarming comments.

857
00:32:36,705 --> 00:32:39,541
I've never enjoyed water sports
here in the Hangang River.

858
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:43,712
It was such an honor to share
this experience with SinB and Dayoung.

859
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:45,130
I loved it.

860
00:32:45,213 --> 00:32:46,631
- Oh, you cutie.
- Thanks.

861
00:32:46,715 --> 00:32:50,302
You're very welcome.

862
00:32:50,385 --> 00:32:52,846
Can we do <i>Hello, Twenty-one - Wonhee</i> next?

863
00:32:52,929 --> 00:32:54,514
- Good idea.
- How's this, then?

864
00:32:54,598 --> 00:32:56,308
<i>Hello, Thirty - Wonhee.</i>

865
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:57,559
WONHEE AS A 30-YEAR-OLD?

866
00:32:57,642 --> 00:32:58,768
<i>Hello, Thirty - Wonhee.</i>

867
00:32:58,977 --> 00:33:01,146
Suppose it gets produced.
What would you do?

868
00:33:01,229 --> 00:33:04,024
I suppose... I could invite you again.

869
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:05,984
- You, Dayoung,
- Sounds lovely.

870
00:33:06,067 --> 00:33:07,611
- and you, SinB.
- Would we be 40?

871
00:33:07,694 --> 00:33:10,030
- I'd be 39.
- We would be...

872
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:12,616
- Let's do that.
- Sounds nice.

873
00:33:12,949 --> 00:33:14,075
Bye.

874
00:33:18,455 --> 00:33:22,918
I seriously feel so blessed.

875
00:33:23,668 --> 00:33:26,421
"TRUST YOURSELF
AND MAKE YOUR MARK ON THE WORLD"

876
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:27,547
WHAT WAS THE SHOW LIKE FOR YOU?

877
00:33:27,631 --> 00:33:30,509
Well, it's my first...

878
00:33:30,592 --> 00:33:32,677
I mean, this is the only year
I get to be 20.

879
00:33:32,761 --> 00:33:34,554
I'm grateful to have so many people

880
00:33:34,638 --> 00:33:37,974
congratulate me and join me
in making amazing memories.

881
00:33:38,058 --> 00:33:41,061
I'm very happy

882
00:33:41,144 --> 00:33:45,106
so many wonderful people
have accompanied me along the way.

883
00:33:45,440 --> 00:33:47,526
Every shoot felt therapeutic.

884
00:33:47,609 --> 00:33:49,361
I'm so grateful to everyone.

885
00:33:49,444 --> 00:33:52,572
ANY CHANGES SINCE EPISODE 1?
Along the way,

886
00:33:52,656 --> 00:33:54,699
I think I've learned to relax.

887
00:33:54,783 --> 00:33:59,037
<i>I was so nervous</i>
<i>and anxious on the first shoot.</i>

888
00:33:59,120 --> 00:34:00,288
What's this?

889
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:07,003
She's the girlie
I've been most excited to meet.

890
00:34:07,087 --> 00:34:07,921
Oh, really?

891
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:10,549
<i>But every shoot became easier for me.</i>

892
00:34:10,632 --> 00:34:12,801
Well done. Be proud of yourself.

893
00:34:16,054 --> 00:34:17,097
This is sick.

894
00:34:19,516 --> 00:34:23,228
<i>Today, I was completely at ease.</i>
<i>It felt like I was in my element.</i>

895
00:34:23,311 --> 00:34:24,771
WHICH ADVICE HAS STUCK WITH YOU?

896
00:34:24,854 --> 00:34:28,900
So many guests have told me
to do whatever I want in my own way.

897
00:34:28,984 --> 00:34:31,736
I plan on following that advice.

898
00:34:31,820 --> 00:34:33,738
A MESSAGE TO FELLOW 20-YEAR-OLDS
My fellow 20-year-olds.

899
00:34:33,822 --> 00:34:38,618
We're all making the most
of our one and only year as 20-year-olds.

900
00:34:38,702 --> 00:34:42,747
I hope you take to heart
the messages my guests have shared.

901
00:34:42,831 --> 00:34:46,167
Believe in yourselves.
Everything will work out.

902
00:34:46,251 --> 00:34:48,044
Keep moving forward.
I'll be cheering you on.

903
00:34:48,128 --> 00:34:49,170
Good luck.

904
00:34:49,254 --> 00:34:53,800
Let's be strong together.

905
00:34:54,593 --> 00:34:57,137
"BELIEVE IN YOURSELF
AND SHINE BRIGHT LIKE THE STARS YOU ARE"

906
00:34:57,220 --> 00:34:59,222
Subtitle translation by Jeongwoo Kim
